{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434047-totems-spirits-of-balance","id":434047,"title":"Totems & Spirits of Balance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T08:05:20-07:00","id":434047,"title":"Totems & Spirits of Balance","content":"Hey, I was wondering if anyone had suggestions on how to build a benevolent spirit totem that's semi-aboriginal. Was inspired by this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ESZeOaAoOH4\" data-code=\"ESZeOaAoOH4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ESZeOaAoOH4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:36:40-07:00","id":434094,"title":"","content":"I'm not quite sure what you're looking for. Visually speaking, spirits look like whatever you want them to. They have very simplified stats. You just need to decide on what Rank they are, and then pick their Influences and Numina from there to make sure they have the powers you think they should have.<br /> <br /> If you're building a Totem, the 2e book has a pretty solid way of translating dots invested into the Totem to the Rank, the number of Attributes, and the number of Numina the spirit has.<br /> <br /> If you want something with as much punch as that video, it's probably going to take a very large pack possibly living in an isolated village where most of the people there are Wolf-blooded pack members (aka a lot of Totem points).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:49:44-07:00","id":434100,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you'd build it like any other spirit. The design could be whatever you want it to be, heck, you can just make it look like Bard if you want. The primary things you'd want to focus on are its influence and it's ban. The ban would probably be something associated with protection or balance. The influence could easily be as simple as plants or earth or water/rain. From what I remember, a lot of Australian aboriginal gods focus on those, especially rain, being a terribly important and scarce commodity in certain parts of Australia.<br /> <br /> If you want to be really thorough you could do some research and draw inspiration from what you find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:22:36-07:00","id":434149,"title":"","content":"Well, with spirits, form generally equals function. If it looks like a train, it'll act like a train. What if it were akin to something like a Maeljin, but specifically bent on Harmonic Balance instead of vice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:58:34-07:00","id":434348,"title":"","content":"Something like that would probably be a lot more powerful than a standard pack totem, but once a spirit gains its independence it's going to find its own form. I guess in this case it does look a little old, so you might have it be an ancient totem that's gone dormant. There are other reasons that would work, since spirits are effectively immortal, but I'd probably do that rather than having a spirit sort of stuck in its rank for centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:28:40-07:00","id":434404,"title":"","content":"If when you say 'like a malejin' you just mean in what it seeks or searches for, there is a bit about conceptual spirits and how they differ from 'standard' symbolic ones (no page ref on hand, sorry) that might help your thinking. Is it Balance for a function, like to promote fairness or equilibrium or such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}